CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--stdlib libc++ --cpp11 --object-bits 12
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ widen: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ narrow: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ widen of a range returns its end: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ widened range: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ narrowed range: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
libc++ defines ctype<char>'s do_widen and do_narrow in its shared library;
without a model the calls of the classic facet returned arbitrary values.
